    "content": "# Block Ops Wiki Go-Live Readiness Matrix\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis page decides what the drafted Block Ops Wiki content can safely become next.\n\nSimple rule:\n\n> The Wiki can go live internally as a draft/review knowledge base, but client-facing and approved-final promotion stays gated by review status.\n\nThis keeps momentum without pretending legal, clinical, platform, or sales-claim-sensitive content is final before review.\n\n## Recommended next move\n\nPromote the drafted Wiki pages into the **internal Block Ops Wiki / Dashboard Wiki** as **review-labeled internal content**.\n\nDo not promote anything to the client portal or approved-final status yet.\n\n## Publishing buckets\n\n### Bucket A \u2014 safe for internal-current draft\n\nThese pages are useful enough to show in the internal Wiki now if clearly labeled as internal and draft/review:\n\n| Page | Internal status | Reviewer | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [[Block Ops Mission]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Uses preferred repeatable site-level program framing. |\n| [[Block Ops Vision]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Internal strategy framing; not client copy yet. |\n| [[Block Ops Positioning and Core Story]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Keep unsupported claims out of final/public language. |\n| [[Pillar Model - Gold Standard Tree]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Six-pillar structure is current; names may be revisited later. |\n| [[Implementation Bundles]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Current term is implementation bundles, not block packs. |\n| [[Block Ops Operating System]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Core layer model is useful now. |\n| [[Roles and Ownership]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Tasks have owners; milestones/workflows do not need owner framing. |\n| [[Mission Control Rules]] | internal-current draft | Samir / Max | Good internal behavior source; verify against live status vocabulary. |\n| [[Weekly Ops Review]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Safe internal operating page. |\n| [[Decision Capture]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Safe internal operating page. |\n| [[Status Rules]] | internal-current draft | Samir / Max | Needs live status vocabulary check before final. |\n| [[Block Ops Wiki - Compendium]] | internal-current draft | Samir / Max | Good internal Wiki concept page. |\n| [[Decision Log - Historical Archive]] | internal-current draft | Samir | Safe internal archive rule page. |\n\n### Bucket B \u2014 internal draft only / business review needed\n\nThese can appear internally, but should stay labeled as draft and review-gated:\n\n| Page | Internal status | Reviewer | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [[Lead Capture]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian / Max | Needs CRM/live-field confirmation. |\n| [[Outreach Sequence]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian | Needs cadence/script validation. |\n| [[CRM Pipeline Stages]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian / Max | Needs live CRM/status alignment. |\n| [[Client Communication Log]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian / Max | Needs schema/logging behavior validation. |\n| [[Qualification and Discovery]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian | Needs real sales/fit review. |\n| [[Proposal Workflow]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian / Max | Pricing/claims/proposal flow not final. |\n| [[Sales Materials and Scripts]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian / legal if external | Contains draft language and claim guardrails. |\n| [[Acquisition - Growth Strategy]] | internal draft | Samir / Adrian | Strategy needs real-market feedback. |\n| [[Client Onboarding]] | internal draft | Samir / Max | Needs live portal/provisioning verification. |\n| [[Implementation Bundle Delivery]] | internal draft | Samir | Delivery model needs review before final/client-facing use. |\n| [[Training Day Readiness]] | internal draft | Samir | Operationally useful; clinical/legal boundaries need review. |\n| [[Go-Live Verification]] | internal draft | Samir / Max | Needs live system and support verification. |\n\n### Bucket C \u2014 restricted / review-gated\n\nThese should be visible only as restricted internal draft material until the right review is complete:\n\n| Page | Internal status | Required gate | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [[Clinical - Block Program Knowledge Index]] | restricted internal draft | Samir clinical fact review | Foundation deliverables need deliverable-by-deliverable review. |\n| [[Legal Review Index]] | restricted internal draft | qualified legal review | Legal package is not final legal truth. |\n| [[Compliance - Risk Controls]] | restricted internal draft | legal + Samir + Max verification | No-PHI, AI, on-site, and claims boundaries need counsel/system confirmation. |\n| [[Supabase Data Model]] | restricted internal draft | Max/live schema verification | SQL/source summary exists, live schema not verified here. |\n| [[Client Portal]] | restricted internal draft | Samir / Max | Client-facing behavior must match approved-final-only rule. |\n| [[Digital Platform Overview]] | internal draft, system-gated | Max | Platform map needs live implementation verification. |\n| [[Dashboard]] | internal draft, system-gated | Max | Needs UI/live behavior verification. |\n| [[Mission Control]] | internal draft, system-gated | Max | Source/seed exists; live Supabase not verified here. |\n| [[Design Handoff Process]] | internal draft | Samir / Max | Safe internally, but needs Max workflow confirmation. |\n| [[Backup and Continuity]] | restricted internal draft | Max backup/restore verification | Actual Supabase/Vercel restore path still needs definition. |\n\n## What can go live now\n\n### Yes \u2014 internal Wiki with labels\n\nThe internal Dashboard Wiki can import these pages if every page preserves:\n\n- page status\n- reviewer / review gate\n- internal-only flag\n- source references\n- no client-facing publication by default\n- no approved-final label unless explicitly reviewed\n\n### No \u2014 client portal\n\nDo not publish these pages or their content to the client portal yet. The portal should only show approved final client-facing content.\n\n### No \u2014 final legal/clinical/source-of-truth claims\n\nDo not call restricted content final until the relevant review is complete.\n\n## Minimum metadata for Max import\n\nIf Max imports these pages into the internal Wiki, each content object should carry:\n\n- title\n- slug\n- source note path\n- area / pillar\n- publish bucket: `internal-current-draft`, `internal-draft`, or `restricted-review-gated`\n- review status\n- reviewer\n- client visible: false\n- approved final: false unless explicitly marked later\n- last updated date\n\n## First review pass order\n\nRecommended sequence:\n\n1. Samir reviews Bucket A for obvious wrong framing.\n2. Max verifies platform pages against live app/Supabase behavior.\n3. Samir + Adrian review sales/client pipeline pages.\n4. Samir reviews delivery and clinical index pages.\n5. Counsel/legal review handles legal/compliance pages before any final use.\n6. After review, promote selected pages from draft to internal-current.\n\n## Related Mission Control workflows/tasks\n\n- M1 Wiki / Compendium promotion\n- M1 Mission Control context linking\n- M2 Legal and Ownership\n- M2 Security and Compliance\n- M2 QA and Validation\n- M2 Portal and Data Flow\n\n## Related wiki pages\n\n- [[Block Ops Wiki Master Content Inventory]]\n- [[Block Ops Wiki Content Migration Plan]]\n- [[Block Ops Wiki - Compendium]]\n- [[Mission Control Rules]]\n- [[Status Rules]]\n- [[Client Portal]]\n\n## Open questions / needs update\n\n- Confirm Max's import path for Obsidian pages into the internal Dashboard Wiki.\n- Confirm whether the internal Wiki supports restricted/review-gated visibility flags yet.\n- Confirm whether Mission Control can link directly to each imported Wiki page after import.\n- Confirm which Bucket A pages Samir wants to mark internal-current first.\n",
